WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.960
There are clues to my past here.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.440
Who am I?

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.510
Where did I come from?

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:33.580
The answers are here.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:40.010
This City Becomes Battle City!

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.160
Yugi?

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.480
There's an exhibit room in the basement?

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:27.780
What's this?

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.560
It's a picture of the ancient Egyptian Pharaoh.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.000
It's definitely me!

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.180
Why is Yugi on this tablet?

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.010
The Millennium Puzzle?

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.440
Anzu.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.850
I now know who I am.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.960
The spirit of the ancient Egyptian Pharaoh that lives inside the Millennium Puzzle.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.490
That's who I am!

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:06.280
Did Yugi get this spirit because he solved the Millennium Puzzle?

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:12.360
Since so much time has passed, no wonder I lost my memories.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.280
I've been waiting for you.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.570
Who are you?

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.980
I am Ishizu Ishtar.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:29.600
For 3,000 years, my family has guarded a portion of the Pharaoh's memories.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:30.720
That's...

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.220
A Millennium Item!

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:37.160
This Millennium Necklace has the power to see the near future.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.940
That's how I knew you were coming here.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.970
And that a new battle will begin.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:52.340
Yes, by coming here of your own free will, your destiny is to battle.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.450
My destiny is to battle?

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.770
You want to regain your memories.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.350
To do so, you must collect all seven Millennium Items.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.700
Get to the point!

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:08.090
Are you my enemy or my ally?

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.480
My Millennium Item is not your enemy.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.440
But I can see who is.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:22.070
An enemy with a new Millennium Item will appear before you soon.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.310
A new Millennium Item?

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:29.550
And you will battle to regain your memories.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.250
Go to the city plaza.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.070
That is where your destiny will begin.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:36.950
What do you mean?

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.350
It's quicker to see for yourself.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.490
Yugi, what's this destiny to battle?

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:54.680
Why is my soul in the Millennium Puzzle?

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:00.160
Why did the seven Millennium Items seal away my memories?

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:05.230
And the other person on this tablet...

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.000
It looks like him.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.320
Can it be?

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:17.330
If it's him, this tablet symbolizes our current state in the present day.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:24.330
In order to solve every mystery, I must restore my memories.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.880
Activating main computer system!

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.220
All systems are green.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.150
Brother, we're ready.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.460
You can start anytime.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:49.960
It's the final test of the next-gen Duel Disk.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.630
Equipping Duel Disk!

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:02.030
Unlike the old version, I don't have to throw this new Disk every turn.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:06.380
By setting a card on the plate, it reads the card data instantly.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:11.820
Our satellite system sends the data to Kaiba Corporation's central computer...

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.640
...which processes the data quickly.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:19.120
It sends the image data back, making the monster three-dimensional.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:25.230
Yugi, you're a noble and unrivaled duelist.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:30.310
When this new Duel Disk is complete, our new battle begins!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:39.100
I don't care if the duelist carved into that ancient tablet is you or not.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:44.850
I will fight you to gain glory in the present and the future!

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.350
Just wait, Yugi!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.360
Duel Robot, standby!

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.610
Duel Robot, standby OK.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.940
Setting tactics level to max.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.280
It's the final test for the new Disk.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:16.450
I don't know if even Seto can defeat the Duel Robot.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.680
You fool!

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.370
My brother will never lose to a computer!

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:27.460
But Mokuba, the Duel Robot will be using Seto's strongest deck.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:32.460
That means three Blue-Eyes White Dragons are in the Duel Robot's deck?

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:35.460
Yes, just as Seto ordered.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:40.870
My brother wants to duel against the most powerful cards?

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:51.790
I entrust Obelisk the Tormentor to you.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:59.290
My deck contains Obelisk the Tormentor, the God Card that Ishizu gave me.

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:05.080
This demonstration is not only the final test of my next-gen Duel Disk...

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.630
...but also to test Obelisk the Tormentor's power.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:21.350
What can this card do against the mightiest deck containing three Blue-Eyes White Dragons?

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:23.790
Let's begin!

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:27.150
Turn on the main computer's Auto Duel System.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:27.980
On!

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.700
Activate Duel Robot!

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.620
Activate!

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.400
Big brother!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.240
Firing Solid Vision Projectors!

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:57.350
Duel!

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:58.350
Bring it!

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.400
My turn.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.170
End Draw Phase.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:04.090
Next is the Main Phase.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.830
I set a card in defense position.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.290
My turn!

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:10.880
I set a card!

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:16.700
I summon Battle Ox in attack position!

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.510
Go, Battle Ox!

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.910
What?  Cyber Jar?

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.780
Cyber Jar's effect activates.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.920
All monsters on the field are destroyed.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:43.650
We both draw five cards from our decks and place all Level 4-or-below monsters on our fields.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.810
Cyber Jar's effect brought a lot of monsters to the field!

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:02.850
My turn.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:09.390
I tribute two Level 4 monsters to summon Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:10.280
What?

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:22.200
Blue-Eyes.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.520
You finally showed up!

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:46.810
I see.  Under the new rules, you must tribute to summon high-Level monsters.

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:50.230
That's why it used Cyber Jar.

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.030
I end my turn.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.530
It's not attacking because it's wary of my set card.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:02.300
It uses excellent strategies because its tactics level is set at max.

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:03.850
It's my turn!

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:08.060
I tribute Hitotsu-Me Giant to summon Dragon Seeker!

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.040
In defense position!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:23.080
When Dragon Seeker switches to attack position, it destroys one Dragon.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.930
It can destroy Blue-Eyes next turn.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:27.930
What will you do?

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.790
My turn.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:34.140
I set one card.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:40.140
Lord of D. in attack position.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:40.810
What?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:52.820
As long as it's faceup on the field, spells, traps and effects can't target Dragon-Type monsters.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.800
It figured out my Dragon Seeker strategy.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.830
I must survive by defending!

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.370
My brother can only defend!

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:09.100
My turn.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:12.940
The Flute of Summoning Dragon.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:22.420
Activating combo.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:28.690
When Lord of D. is faceup, I can place up to two Dragons in my hand on the field.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:29.740
What?

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:30.860
Big brother!

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:39.700
Three Blue-Eyes!

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:42.160
I flip over my set card.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:47.880
I use Polymerization to fuse three Blue-Eyes into Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:49.380
What?

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:03.840
Under the new rules, if I fuse, I can't attack that turn.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:06.130
I end my turn.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.500
Beautiful.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:15.670
Big brother!

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.020
It's impossible!

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:21.310
There's no way to defeat Ultimate Dragon!

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:24.680
If he's attacked, he'll take physical damage!

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:25.350
What?

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:30.880
Seto's Duel Disk is set up so that he can actually feel the attack damage!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.360
Brother, it's too dangerous!

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:36.980
Stop the duel!

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.100
Big brother!

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.280
Yugi.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:56.220
Yugi, did you always feel this fear when you were facing me?

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:02.520
But you never hesitated to face this fear.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:05.740
By believing in your cards.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:12.200
A duelist's biggest enemy is the fear inside his heart known as...

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.630
...a monster!

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.270
My turn!

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:27.070
I'm betting everything on this card!

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:32.950
Come, Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.560
I tribute three monsters on my field!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:57.740
Is that the God Card my brother was talking about?

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:02.320
This is my ultimate weapon, Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.820
Unleash your powers to the fullest!

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:17.300
Absorb my two monsters' soul power!

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:22.700
Big trouble!  Its attack points are rapidly increasing!

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.200
Forgive me, Ultimate Dragon.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:30.800
This God will make you rest in peace.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:32.940
Obelisk, attack!

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:36.950
Obelisk, God Hand Crusher!

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.960
System error...

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.360
Danger...

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.120
The Duel Robot!

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.700
The main computer is out of control!

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:05.370
Obelisk the Tormentor eliminated the player's life points in an instant.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.620
Magnificent.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:14.050
No matter who stands in my way, I'll get the remaining two God Cards!

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:19.060
And I'll become the true Duel King!

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:33.760
Anzu.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:34.700
What?

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:39.370
My partner doesn't know that I saw the tablet today.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:44.230
Can you keep the tablet and what Ishizu said a secret?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:50.560
Even if I get my memories back, I don't know if I can stay with my partner.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.900
I don't want him to worry for no reason.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:03.760
We always build my deck together.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.230
His soul makes up half of this deck.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:15.660
When he truly understands me, this deck will unleash its true power.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.380
I'm sure that time will come.

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:25.340
Strange...

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.850
I keep sensing a threat.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.270
What's wrong?

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:31.860
You look angry.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:34.000
It's nothing.

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.220
Hey Yugi!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.280
Mai Kujaku!

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.030
Mai?

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:42.170
Long time no see!  How are you?

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:44.540
You're full of energy, like usual.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:47.420
Oh whatever.  Anyway...

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.140
Anzu, you're dating Yugi?

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:53.770
It's not like that.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.280
You're blushing!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.020
Mai, I give up!

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.620
Mai, why are you here?

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.220
Why?

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.460
You came here without knowing why?

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:09.800
Yeah.  I was told that coming here will lead to my future.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:11.460
The future...

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:12.700
You may be right.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:17.260
There was a message on the internet a few days ago.

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:25.110
"Duelists, gather at the city where ancient duelists and card carvings sleep."

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:28.850
Ancient duelists and card carvings?

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:36.590
The date and time is right now.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:40.560
There will be an announcement for a huge duel tournament.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:41.830
Duel tournament?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.830
Yugi, you must have noticed.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:49.840
Yeah.  I sense threats throughout this plaza that can only come from duelists.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:54.710
Yes.  They're duelists that have come from all over the country.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:58.080
You should see some people that you know.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:03.080
That's Insector Haga!

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.920
And Dinosaur Ryuzaki!

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:05.950
Yes.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.420
And that's psychic duelist Esper Roba!

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.260
Even Ryota Kajiki is here!

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.750
I see.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:17.000
These duelists heard the message and gathered here.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.250
Yugi, look!

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:22.530
Kaiba!

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:36.560
Rumors say that he's the one who sent the message.

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:38.720
Kaiba is hosting the tournament?

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:41.980
Duelists, listen closely!

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:48.460
Kaiba Corporation will host a Duel Monsters tournament in this city a week from today.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:53.070
Duelists must meet two requirements to enter.

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:57.000
You must have a 40-card deck that includes rare cards.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:01.680
And you must own this next-gen Duel Disk.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:03.680
What is that?

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.980
Is it a new product from Kaiba Corporation?

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.500
We'll play using Battle City rules.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.720
And the ante rule.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:16.990
The loser must give the rarest card in his deck to the winner.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.230
Ante your rarest card?

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:23.230
Kaiba uses harsh rules.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:28.620
This means the tournament winner will acquire many rare cards!

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:29.910
Wow!

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:31.370
Where's the arena?

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:39.410
Kaiba!

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:44.420
I knew you'd come, Yugi.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:48.170
We'll settle our destiny in this battle!

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:54.430
The tournament will take place throughout Domino City!

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:58.920
In a week, this city will become Battle City!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.000
Battle City?

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:06.570
Battle City.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.340
Yes, Marik.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:12.410
Duelists throughout the country are gathering at Domino City.

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:19.840
How convenient that our prey are gathering in a single location.

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:24.260
Bring home the Ghouls' Rare Hunters from all over the world!

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:29.190
Our next target is Domino City!

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:43.920
Jonouchi is determined to participate in Battle City.

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:48.350
But only Kaiba-approved duelists can get a Duel Disk.

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:50.620
What?  Jonouchi can get one?

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.800
Congrats!

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:55.500
Duel Disk in hand, Jonouchi rushes to see Shizuka at the hospital.

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.170
The Ghouls ambush him?

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.920
That's bad!  The surgery is about to start!

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:05.050
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Ghouls Attack
Red-Eyes B. Dragon Targeted

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:06.600
Duel, standby!

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:25.160
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:30.530
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.070 --> 00:22:40.210
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:51.720
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:54.590 --> 00:22:59.230
Time passes bit by bit

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:04.500
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:09.610
Will never change

00:23:10.270 --> 00:23:14.880
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:20.080
To be who I am

00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:25.320
I've kept searching for something

00:23:25.990 --> 00:23:30.030
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:32.960
I learned that's the answer

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:40.070
From now until forever...
